name: not_caught_no_final_choice
description: >-
  A match whose choices are all conditional. The compiler accepts it and the
  output type becomes optional(list(string)); the supported profile refuses
  it (celcheck's restricted-profile check), because the evaluator then needs
  the optional extension and no match would not mean UNKNOWN.
rule:
  match:
    - condition: iteration == "commit"
      output: '["form_check"]'
